review_comments:
- Subscription upkeep and MTU exchange are unrelated. We should keep it separate in code as well.
- It's simpler if enabling automatic MTU exchange depends only on `CONFIG_BT_GATT_AUTO_UPDATE_MTU`. That is what that kconfig's name means to me.
- It's more correct if this fails to compile if `depends on BT_GATT_CLIENT` is removed from `CONFIG_BT_GATT_AUTO_UPDATE_MTU` but `bt_gatt_exchange_mtu` is not defined instead of silently ignoring `CONFIG_BT_GATT_AUTO_UPDATE_MTU`.

```suggestion
#endif /* CONFIG_BT_GATT_CLIENT */

#if defined(CONFIG_BT_GATT_AUTO_UPDATE_MTU)
	int err;

	err = bt_gatt_exchange_mtu(conn, &gatt_exchange_params);
	if (err) {
		BT_WARN("MTU Exchange failed (err %d)", err);
	}
#endif /* CONFIG_BT_GATT_AUTO_UPDATE_MTU */
```
